                "entry_id": "2208b2d7-863b-3385-b799-3516f0f5bdc6",
                "word": "retransition",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "dc1a5320-fd64-424a-84e3-aee49e25f9d2",
                        "entry_id": "2208b2d7-863b-3385-b799-3516f0f5bdc6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "retransitions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af526d10-9858-3695-8375-c1bedacb45f0",
                        "entry_id": "2208b2d7-863b-3385-b799-3516f0f5bdc6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Retour vers le genre initial après avoir effectué ou commencé une transition de genre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Transitude"
                        ],
                        "note": "Ce terme est parfois préféré à détransition (plus courant), afin de mettre en avant que la nouvelle transition ne s’oppose pas à la précédente mais est partie intégrante d'un même parcours",
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60364957-a31b-4b25-a2f9-192aebbb1b7f",
                                "sense_id": "af526d10-9858-3695-8375-c1bedacb45f0",
                                "text": "Une détransition ou une retransition peut engendrer un changement d’identité, de présentation sociale, de documents administratifs, ou une transition médicale."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf8227fe-1bd4-40ae-8d7d-9a3cd5087fe2",
                        "source_entry_id": "2208b2d7-863b-3385-b799-3516f0f5bdc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "af526d10-9858-3695-8375-c1bedacb45f0",
                        "target_lang_word": "retransition",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "retransition",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "988f6bec-3354-3e98-bb85-a36f8e8f9e05",
                                        "entry_id": "679fb6b1-3fa6-348a-9b75-349dcbb107f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Another transition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a52d64f1-3d60-4bad-81af-e57c3367d0cb",
                                                "sense_id": "988f6bec-3354-3e98-bb85-a36f8e8f9e05",
                                                "text": "The content of the development is harder to define; it may include new material, but typically involves development of motives and themes from the exposition leading to a retransition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "retransition",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "015499dc-07a1-398a-9f20-399e75ba306c",
                                        "entry_id": "6022bbd6-6827-3ae8-9b25-5675acc55f4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transition again.",
                                            "To undergo another transition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f74409e2-6acf-48e0-96ac-1b6476c2c67d",
                                                "sense_id": "015499dc-07a1-398a-9f20-399e75ba306c",
                                                "text": "With apologies to my friends who have detransitioned or retransitioned if I get this wrong, this is what I've learned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72fbfa72-bf26-4362-b7ce-5d858cea8b2a",
                                                "sense_id": "015499dc-07a1-398a-9f20-399e75ba306c",
                                                "text": "One reason for encouraging detransitioners to go through counselling and avoid rushing into further surgery is that many go on to retransition again in the future."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0aa550a-de2e-4847-9c7a-d6866c5f9221",
                                                "sense_id": "015499dc-07a1-398a-9f20-399e75ba306c",
                                                "text": "She also observes that within the number of those who detransition, a significant proportion do so due to how intense their experiences of rejection and transphobia are – and so then actually retransition further on in life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c425781-affb-45ee-b501-5b48ad958b5c",
                                                "sense_id": "015499dc-07a1-398a-9f20-399e75ba306c",
                                                "text": "Included in this group were 4 individuals (1.3% of the total sample) who retransitioned twice (to nonbinary then back to binary transgender). Some youth (3.5%) were currently living as nonbinary, including one who had retransitioned first to cisgender then to nonbinary. Finally, 2.5% were using pronouns associated with their sex at birth and could be categorized as cisgender at the time of data collection, including one who first retransitioned to live as nonbinary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab6a069f-9f16-3c9d-95b2-1bff6f5d2abe",
                                        "entry_id": "6022bbd6-6827-3ae8-9b25-5675acc55f4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transition again.",
                                            "To return to one's birth-assigned gender after having undergone gender reassignment; to detransition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abd87bb9-23cb-4413-af02-76e31e26b950",
                                                "sense_id": "ab6a069f-9f16-3c9d-95b2-1bff6f5d2abe",
                                                "text": "Finally, some who embrace the psychological paradigm critique transition-affirmative approaches by pointing to studies showing that a statistically significant number of people who have undergone transition – one 2009 study suggests up to 8 percent – have later expressed regrets, with some even deciding to retransition back to their birth sex."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a05aac1-92e0-4ba7-87fc-458923dbf7f0",
                                                "sense_id": "ab6a069f-9f16-3c9d-95b2-1bff6f5d2abe",
                                                "text": "If a socially transitioned child desists and later comes to identify with their birth-assigned gender, the child must then retransition to that gender, which could be difficult and pose risks for the child at that older age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3403392e-b9e9-4350-8fe0-24248da7077e",
                                                "sense_id": "ab6a069f-9f16-3c9d-95b2-1bff6f5d2abe",
                                                "text": "In some cases, individuals may “detransition” (or retransition) to their assigned/biological gender, further complicating identity and family relationships."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
